  <language>en_US</language>
  <keyword>morse.practice</keyword>
  <short_description>Open the interactive Morse trainer.</short_description>
  <syntax>
    <syntax_item>morse.practice()</syntax_item>
    <syntax_item>h = morse.practice()</syntax_item>
  </syntax>
  <param_input />
  <param_output>
    <param_output_item>
      <param_name>h</param_name>
      <param_description>the handle of the trainer window.</param_description>
    </param_output_item>
  </param_output>
  <description>
    <p>Opens a single window where you type a message, see it turn into Morse in a radio-style readout, and send it to the speaker. The code speed, the overall (Farnsworth) speed and the tone frequency are adjustable; lowering the overall speed below the code speed stretches the spacing while the elements stay crisp. The audio can be saved to a WAV file, and the full code table is one click away. Needs a graphical display.</p>
  </description>
